{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:63b2e49124926586","name":"SD-6 \"Hulk\" Infantry Droid Squad","source":{"id":"source:reference-63b2e49124926586","title":"SD-6 \"Hulk\" Infantry Droid Squad","revision":23230,"timestamp":"2024-09-20T14:08:39Z","sha256":"116d6138ecc81900f1297f1814be802ab5725620ab84b6cfc5a779b472be5f9f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=23230","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=SD-6%20%22Hulk%22%20Infantry%20Droid%20Squad&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-63b2e49124926586","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dawn of Defiance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dawn_of_Defiance"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["The Gem of Alderaan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Gem_of_Alderaan","referenceId":"reference:af655fda4f1d1f00"},"), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The New Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_New_Republic","referenceId":"reference:e6046dbb57e5abb0"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["This massive War Droid is layered in heavy armor, and it mounts an ",{"tag":"a","children":["E-Web Repeating Blaster"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/E-Web_Repeating_Blaster","referenceId":"reference:3bac50ec8614d1fb"}," and an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion Rifle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion_Rifle","referenceId":"reference:a21c35934de9acbe"}," on each shoulder."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Balmorran Arms SD-6 \"Hulk\" Infantry Droid is one of the most lethal Droids on the market. Designed ostensibly for security purposes, the SD-6 is often used in private militaries and mercenary units as weapons of war. The SD-6 has been in service for years, and the militaries of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["The New Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_New_Republic","referenceId":"reference:e6046dbb57e5abb0"}," all used these Droids throughout major conflicts (though ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"}," did set the Droids aside during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", for fear of confusion with Separatist forces).\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The SD-6 is a formidable Droid that boasts twin ",{"tag":"a","children":["E-Web Repeating Blasters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/E-Web_Repeating_Blasters"}," and twin ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion Rifles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion_Rifles"}," attached to its upper appendages, allowing It to unleash a torrent of blaster fire on its enemies. Despite the presence of this dangerous weapons load, the SD-6 still finds its way into the hands of private citizens, and is often used to guard hangars and docking bays where the presence of heavy weaponry is a deterrent to would-be intruders.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["SD-6 \"Hulk\" Infantry Droid Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["War Droids of all kinds, including the SD-6 Infantry Droid, are typically more destructive and rare than more run-of-the-mill Battle Droids. That fact aside, War Droid encounters might use a large number of low-level ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," Battle Droids while featuring a single War Droid or a pair of them to serve as the Battle Droids' commanders. Similarly, a War Droid encounter that also features low-level ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldiers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldiers_(CL_2)"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Brutes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Brutes"},", or any other warrior type presents a variety of challenges, including the decision of when to whittle down the support troops and when to take out the lumbering War Droid.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["War Droids can also be found in the possession of crime lords and other powerful criminals. Not caring for the legalities of owning a War Droid, many crime lords pick up these War Droids secondhand from governments and use them as personal security. War Droids, which are significantly tougher than Battle Droids, can usually act as an entire illegal security force, and many crime lords use War Droids to protect their personal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," from shipjackers and other thieves. An encounter with a War Droid featuring a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Crime Lord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Crime_Lord_(CL_12)","referenceId":"reference:256c54e67879250d"}," will usually also include some of the Crime Lord's minions (low-level ",{"tag":"a","children":["Brutes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Brutes"}," and other criminals) and a lieutenant or other more powerful minion.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["SD-6 \"Hulk\" Infantry Droid"],"href